  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758587,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "### 007: The Duel - Sega Mega Drive/Genesis\n\nStep into the shoes of James Bond in *007: The Duel*, a side-scrolling action game for the Sega Mega Drive/Genesis! Developed and published by Domark in 1993, this unique Bond title breaks from the traditional movie and novel adaptations, presenting an entirely original storyline.\n\nEquipped with a trusty pistol, players guide Bond through perilous enemy bases, battling waves of thugs and iconic villains like Jaws and Oddjob. The mission? Rescue female hostages and strategically arm a bomb to destroy each base. Gameplay involves navigating challenging side-scrolling levels, utilizing Bond’s skills to overcome obstacles and defeat formidable bosses.\n\nNotably, *The Duel* features Timothy Dalton’s final appearance as James Bond, showcased prominently in the opening screens. While the narrative isn't its strongest element, the game's originality paved the way for future Bond games to explore original storylines, influencing subsequent developers like EA. Experience a classic Bond adventure with a fresh perspective in this action-packed Sega Mega Drive/Genesis title."
    },
